=== Text #1 ===
> The home includes four bedrooms[,] three baths,[ a cozy] living[ room with large] picture windows[ and a beautiful stone] fire place[, a spacious dining room, a] fully[ equipped] kitchen[, a] multi level wrap[ around deck] just yards from the creek[,] a sauna[ and] a[ large laundry] room. The equipment in the kitchen[ includes: coffee] maker[,] range[ and] oven, refrigerator[,] microwave[,] toaster[,] garbage disposal[ and] compactor[, and] all dishes, pot and pans. Two of the bedrooms[ have] queen beds ([one also has] deck access), and two bedrooms[ have] two twin beds. The entire home is decorated in a Native American/Western motif and furnished with modern, rustic wood furniture. There is[ a wonderful] library of books,[ a] well[ equipped] stereo system[ and] several[ large] window seats on the man floor to complete the comfortable setting. This home sleeps eight.
Directions: This home is set in a gorgeous location about five miles southwest of Red Lodge off of West Fork Road. It is located on one of the primary waterways in the Red Lodge area, the West Fork of Rock Creek, which drains the western side of the Beartooth Wilderness. The home is a beautiful log lodge style home and includes a[ huge], multi[ level deck that] stops just a few yards from the water's edge. There are several places to explore up and down the creek and a number of hiking trails and roads in the area. This is a perfect way to enjoy Red Lodge, or to just relax, enjoy the solitude and get away from the world.

=== Text #2 ===
> A Belize City woman who pleaded guilty to one count of drug[ trafficking] when she appeared before Chief Mag[istrate] Ann Marie Smith today was fined the mandatory minimum sentence of $10,000.
Smith ordered her to pay $5,000 immediately; in default, she will have to begin serving the three-year prison sentence the offense carries.
The woman, Roshawn Higgs[,] 35[,] a domestic of #6 -7th Street[,] Kings Park[,] who is the mother of five children, the[ youngest] being one-year old, is a first-time[ offender].
In court, an unrepresented Higgs said she was guilty of possession[,] but the Chief Magistrate told her that the charge before the court was for drug trafficking.
When Smith asked her to enter a plea, Higgs pleaded guilty to the one count of drug trafficking.
Higgs was arrested and charged[ after a] police search of[ her] home on Tuesday, April 8, led to the[ discovery of the] 150[ grams of] cannabis.
According to the police report of the incident, around 5:30 p.m[.,] PC Carl Garbutt was on patrol in the Kings Park[ area].
Garbutt searched[ a dark-skinned man who was standing under] a[ tree] in[ a yard].[ The] search[,] however, did not yield anything incriminating on the man.
But then Garbutt reported that he saw[ a woman standing by the door] of[ a house] in the yard[,] and she[ was] acting suspiciously, so he decided that he would search her house for illegal firearms and drugs.
During the search of Higgs’ room, Garbutt found[ a] barrel[ and] inside it was[ a blue container with] three plastic bags. The bags contained a[ green] leafy substance suspected to[ be] cannabis.
Garbutt said he cautioned Higgs before arresting her, and took her to the police station where the[ suspected] cannabis was weighed in her presence, and it amounted to 150 grams, which is less than a half pound of weed.
Higgs was unable to pay the $5,000 fine and was sent to Belize Central Prison to begin serving her sentence. If she can pay the $5,000 fine, however, she will be released and can seek an extension from the court for payment of the other $5,000.

=== Text #3 ===
> Master Bedroom--[Imagine] waking up[ to] looking out over[ the] water!
This never gets old.....another gorgeous sunset!
Beach[:] Beach and sand flats are about 40 feet away.
LOCATION: Enjoy your stay on this beautiful pond located in West Tisbury on the gorgeous island of Martha's Vineyard. Tisbury Great Pond is an exceptional, private, quiet sanctuary away from everything. It is where the surf rolls in across the landscape. The pond offers an abundance of activities and places to explore. When[ the] ''cut'' is open, it is the absolute best. The beach offers numerous sand flats for the young ones to play on, the water is extremely warm and shallow, but also has deep places to swim. Then there is surfing available on the ocean side. When the ''[cut]'' is open, you can ride in or[ out] depending on which way the tide is going......It is magical!! This is the place to reconnect with nature and be totally at peace. While everything else to make your Vineyard vacation wonderful is not far away, when you are here, you are far, far away in your own, off-the-grid world.
Drive down approximately 3 miles on a[ dirt] road, and this will lead you to the house. The house sits on a 3.5[ acre] parcel on the west side of Middle Point and overlooks Thumb and Deep Bottom Coves. The immediate area is a globally-rare, sand plain, containing grassland[ and] heath[ which] extends out to the barrier beach and the ocean.
The[ property] includes a[ beach and] swimming area on the Pond[,] where one can pull up and store canoes[,] kayaks, sailboats, (Sunfish, Laser are available). A[ canoe] is[ available] for exploring the pond and paddling to the barrier beach. To further enhance your stay, sailboats and kayaks can be rented from Winds Up on the Beach Road in Vineyard Haven.
THE HOUSE: The house[ has] (4[)] four bedrooms[ and] ([1)] full bath[. Each] of the four bedrooms[ can] accommodate 2 people[.] Bedroom #[1 has a double] bed[,] bedroom #[2 has a double bed,] bedroom #[3 has twin beds], and bedroom #[4 has twin beds.] But these bedrooms are unlike anything you have ever seen! Everything is built in, and the overall effect is as if you were on a ship. The twin beds[ are] not one on top of another,[ but rather they are] perpendicular to each other, affording each person their own privacy and space.

